.git
.github
bin
site
docs
# Not excluded, unlike the documentation it was collected for: the interface's
# brand files are symlinks into it, so an excluded assets/ leaves them dangling
# and the web build fails.
*.md

# Installed by a local build, and the stage that needs it runs `npm ci` for
# itself. Copied in, it lands on top of what that stage installed and the build
# fails on a file replacing a directory — so the image built only on a machine
# that had never built the interface.
web/node_modules

# Both are interface builds, and the image makes its own. Copied in, they are
# not replaced: the web stage's output lands on top, and a chunk whose name
# carries a content hash does not collide with the stale one beside it — so
# every asset from every local build the developer ever ran stays in the
# binary, reachable by address and referenced by nothing. Measured at 191 dead
# files and 3.4 MB on one machine, and the binary embeds the directory whole.
web/dist
internal/webui/dist
